1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
[English subtitles are available]

2
00:00:05,450 --> 00:00:09,850
[Once upon a time, there was a lake.]

3
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:15,610
[The elder in the tribe
warned the youngsters]

4
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:21,200
[to never go near the lake.]

5
00:00:21,330 --> 00:00:29,300
[One day, an outsider passed by the lake.]

6
00:00:29,390 --> 00:00:34,840
[He accidentally dropped a stone
into the water.]

7
00:00:34,970 --> 00:00:38,800
[When the stone fell into the water,]

8
00:00:38,930 --> 00:00:41,050
[it created ripples in the lake.]

9
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:44,610
[The man then saw the future]

10
00:00:44,740 --> 00:00:50,420
[through the reflection in the water.]

11
00:00:50,510 --> 00:00:54,160
[In the future,]

12
00:00:54,250 --> 00:00:57,370
[he would have a good harvest.]

13
00:00:57,460 --> 00:01:01,680
[He would buy a lot of rice fields]

14
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:05,820
[and live a comfortable life.]

15
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:16,510
[The man never thought
he could see the future.]

16
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:18,710
[He gradually became addicted to it.]

17
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:26,450
[Every day, the man would come
to the lake to throw stones.]

18
00:01:26,580 --> 00:01:28,390
[He stopped plowing the fields]

19
00:01:28,520 --> 00:01:32,520
[and only cared
about throwing stones by the lake.]

20
00:01:32,660 --> 00:01:36,180
[In the end,
the man's field was laid waste]

21
00:01:36,259 --> 00:01:41,280
[and his savings ran dry.]

22
00:01:41,370 --> 00:01:45,550
[Eventually, people realized]

23
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:51,310
[the reflection
that the man saw in the lake]

24
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:55,710
[wasn't his future at all.]

25
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:59,060
[It was a curse from a Kariah.]

26
00:02:01,170 --> 00:02:02,930
This is...

27
00:02:03,020 --> 00:02:04,730
My wife's notebook.

28
00:02:07,190 --> 00:02:08,470
It's empty.

29
00:02:09,530 --> 00:02:11,460
This isn't an ordinary notebook.

30
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:16,829
[Today's to-do list.]

31
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:18,850
[First, confirm the Kawas
evacuation schedule.]

32
00:02:18,940 --> 00:02:21,010
[Revise the location
for the seventh evacuation.]

33
00:02:21,140 --> 00:02:22,680
Is this her work log?

34
00:02:22,810 --> 00:02:25,890
Yes, it's her work log
at the Cause and Effect Correction Bureau.

35
00:02:27,079 --> 00:02:28,140
Read this part first.

36
00:02:34,170 --> 00:02:38,390
[Two weeks before the last rainfall]

37
00:02:59,860 --> 00:03:01,580
How far along are we

38
00:03:01,710 --> 00:03:03,210
on the timeline of Reflection of Time?

39
00:03:03,290 --> 00:03:04,000
The messenger, 'Orad,

40
00:03:04,130 --> 00:03:05,580
has found Raka

41
00:03:05,670 --> 00:03:07,380
according to timeline number 34587

42
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:08,920
[of the Reflection of Time.]

43
00:03:17,590 --> 00:03:18,690
[The messenger, 'Orad,]

44
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:20,280
[has gotten onto Raka's car.]

45
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:23,270
[He'll get an executor
to take her into custody.]

46
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:33,650
What about the precursor
in timeline number 34601?

47
00:03:33,780 --> 00:03:35,280
Where are we at so far?

48
00:03:35,370 --> 00:03:36,780
Reporting.

49
00:03:36,860 --> 00:03:40,160
Regarding the current timeline
number 34601,

50
00:03:40,250 --> 00:03:42,980
[we need to let
Chen Ai-ting and Chen Ai-yu]

51
00:03:43,070 --> 00:03:44,120
[bump into Hsieh Tien-ti]

52
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:47,420
[at the set time according to the plan.]

53
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:49,230
[We will be sending
a memory modification agent]

54
00:03:49,320 --> 00:03:51,560
[to carry out
the prerequisite modification work.]

55
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:55,040
[Okay, good.]

56
00:03:55,170 --> 00:03:58,070
According to timeline number 34601,

57
00:03:58,200 --> 00:03:59,610
provide some instructions to Chen Ai-yu.

58
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:00,620
The arrangement has been made for her

59
00:04:00,710 --> 00:04:01,860
to run away from the kindergarten

60
00:04:01,940 --> 00:04:03,440
in order to look for Raka.

61
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:05,330
This wraps up the precursory assignments

62
00:04:05,420 --> 00:04:08,060
for these timelines.

63
00:04:09,510 --> 00:04:10,740
Once the messenger, 'Orad,

64
00:04:10,830 --> 00:04:12,060
applies for the Comb of Memories

65
00:04:12,280 --> 00:04:13,430
and carries out the rest of the plan,

66
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:14,570
we can call it a day.

67
00:04:22,970 --> 00:04:24,870
Other than everyone's current job,

68
00:04:24,950 --> 00:04:26,230
I have another very important task

69
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:27,810
to delegate to you.

70
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:30,190
There are only two weeks left

71
00:04:30,280 --> 00:04:32,350
before the date of our evacuation.

72
00:04:32,430 --> 00:04:34,370
Before you get off work today,

73
00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:36,130
go through all the records

74
00:04:36,220 --> 00:04:37,670
that are going into the archive.

75
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:42,470
Didn't you hear me?

76
00:04:43,650 --> 00:04:45,060
Move!

77
00:04:51,440 --> 00:04:52,630
Your two stacks of documents

78
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:53,380
are different.

79
00:04:53,470 --> 00:04:53,950
They're in the same box.

80
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:56,370
Will you be able to find them later?

81
00:04:57,340 --> 00:04:58,480
Two weeks.

82
00:04:58,610 --> 00:05:01,030
There are only two weeks left.

83
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:02,000
There's not much time left.

84
00:05:02,130 --> 00:05:04,690
Please pay attention!

85
00:05:04,770 --> 00:05:07,110
You've worked hard, Malusakadat.

86
00:05:09,130 --> 00:05:10,450
Why are you here?

87
00:05:10,580 --> 00:05:11,990
I came to get the comb.

88
00:05:14,500 --> 00:05:18,500
[Episode 11, The Reflection of Time]

89
00:06:48,960 --> 00:06:50,240
[Emptiness]

90
00:06:52,350 --> 00:06:53,760
Which part are you at?

91
00:06:55,080 --> 00:06:57,450
I'm on number 34638.

92
00:06:58,250 --> 00:06:59,210
It's the part

93
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:01,020
where I went to look for you
at the university

94
00:07:01,150 --> 00:07:03,000
to persuade you to go back to Pinokayan.

95
00:07:03,440 --> 00:07:04,450
When I read this part,

96
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:06,250
I was almost scared to death.

97
00:07:06,390 --> 00:07:06,830
We all know

98
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:08,410
that my wife is a bit of a control freak.

99
00:07:08,500 --> 00:07:10,300
But I didn't know she would go that far.

100
00:07:10,570 --> 00:07:12,060
She didn't just note down what you did,

101
00:07:12,150 --> 00:07:13,730
but everything I did as well.

102
00:07:15,360 --> 00:07:17,160
The job of the Cause and Effect
Correction Bureau

103
00:07:17,250 --> 00:07:18,400
is to correct the things

104
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:20,600
that diverged from Kakarayan's plan.

105
00:07:20,770 --> 00:07:23,590
So it makes sense
to put everything on record.

106
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:27,680
But something isn't right.

107
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:30,580
Right? This bit here is strange.

108
00:07:30,890 --> 00:07:33,050
[Timeline number 34638.]

109
00:07:33,140 --> 00:07:35,250
[Make Li Pu-hui
test the messenger, 'Orad,]

110
00:07:35,340 --> 00:07:36,520
[regarding the evacuation]

111
00:07:36,659 --> 00:07:37,620
[and confirm his current thoughts]

112
00:07:37,710 --> 00:07:40,350
[on Kakarayan's arrangement.]

113
00:07:41,580 --> 00:07:43,260
What god of creation?

114
00:07:44,270 --> 00:07:45,760
He's just a typical boss.

115
00:07:46,510 --> 00:07:47,350
No.

116
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:51,000
He's worse than a typical boss.

117
00:07:51,130 --> 00:07:52,409
He's the most powerful in heaven.

118
00:07:52,500 --> 00:07:53,820
No one can tell Him what to do.

119
00:07:58,080 --> 00:07:58,659
'Orad.

120
00:07:59,490 --> 00:08:01,120
I think it's almost time.

121
00:08:01,300 --> 00:08:02,660
Why don't I go and buy...

122
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:10,540
Okay.

123
00:08:12,380 --> 00:08:13,310
I'll go get another bottle.

124
00:08:15,330 --> 00:08:18,370
Yes, I was the one
who asked you out for a drink that day.

125
00:08:18,670 --> 00:08:20,520
I only wanted to hear the messenger

126
00:08:20,610 --> 00:08:22,680
complain about Kakarayan.

127
00:08:22,850 --> 00:08:23,380
But...

128
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,410
why does it seem like a lot of things

129
00:08:25,670 --> 00:08:27,340
written in this notebook

130
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:30,110
were planned
by the Cause and Effect Correction Bureau

131
00:08:30,470 --> 00:08:32,530
and I was going through with it
without realizing?

132
00:08:33,940 --> 00:08:35,530
That's not the strangest part though.

133
00:08:35,830 --> 00:08:37,070
The strangest thing

134
00:08:37,419 --> 00:08:38,390
is underneath this record,

135
00:08:38,909 --> 00:08:40,500
my wife wrote something else.

136
00:08:41,770 --> 00:08:43,710
[According to the findings,
the messenger, 'Orad,]

137
00:08:43,840 --> 00:08:46,040
[is currently very dissatisfied
with Kakarayan.]

138
00:08:47,710 --> 00:08:49,870
You're an adult. Take care of yourself.

139
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:51,940
Why did you drink
when you can't hold your liquor?

140
00:08:54,140 --> 00:08:55,370
Seriously.

141
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:57,750
No matter how reluctant you are,

142
00:08:58,230 --> 00:08:59,420
as a Kawas,

143
00:08:59,510 --> 00:09:00,430
there's only one thing we can do.

144
00:09:00,690 --> 00:09:02,410
Forget it. It's no use talking about it.

145
00:09:04,610 --> 00:09:06,240
I'll drink it if you can't.

146
00:09:06,370 --> 00:09:07,430
Here, cheers.

147
00:09:12,880 --> 00:09:13,810
I said I'd drink it,

148
00:09:13,890 --> 00:09:15,520
so you're really letting me
drink it alone.

149
00:09:15,650 --> 00:09:17,590
[-PS. Li Pu-hui failed to follow orders.]
-Fine.

150
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:19,660
[He let the messenger drink too much]

151
00:09:19,740 --> 00:09:21,110
[and caused him to suddenly disappear,]

152
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:22,380
[veering off the plan.]

153
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:25,200
He's such an unreliable guy.

154
00:09:25,290 --> 00:09:26,390
[What did you say?]

155
00:09:27,220 --> 00:09:28,900
'Orad got drunk and disappeared,

156
00:09:28,980 --> 00:09:30,570
and now, you don't know where he went?

157
00:09:34,130 --> 00:09:35,230
That Pu-hui.

158
00:09:35,720 --> 00:09:37,560
He was only supposed
to take 'Orad out for a meal.

159
00:09:37,650 --> 00:09:39,240
No one said to make him drunk.

160
00:09:39,680 --> 00:09:42,270
What should I do
with the change of plan now?

161
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:45,350
Malusakadat.

162
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:46,580
The messenger, 'Orad,

163
00:09:46,670 --> 00:09:48,340
just appeared at Hsieh Tien-ti's house.

164
00:09:48,430 --> 00:09:49,360
That isn't

165
00:09:49,440 --> 00:09:50,460
in the original timeline.

166
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:52,130
What should we do now?

167
00:09:53,670 --> 00:09:55,470
I'll take care of it.

168
00:09:57,060 --> 00:09:58,900
It went a little off the path,

169
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:00,400
but it won't affect

170
00:10:00,580 --> 00:10:02,730
the relationship
between 'Orad and Hsieh Tien-ti.

171
00:10:03,350 --> 00:10:03,830
We will proceed

172
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:06,430
with the plan made
according to the timeline.

173
00:10:10,700 --> 00:10:12,060
[We decided to go
with Fali's instructions.]

174
00:10:12,190 --> 00:10:13,780
[Despite it veering off
the intended path,]

175
00:10:13,860 --> 00:10:15,010
[it doesn't affect the feeling]

176
00:10:15,100 --> 00:10:16,330
['Orad will have toward Hsieh Tien-ti.]

177
00:10:16,500 --> 00:10:16,990
[Everything is going]

178
00:10:17,120 --> 00:10:19,320
[according to the planned timeline.]

179
00:10:22,620 --> 00:10:24,290
"Go with Fali's instructions."

180
00:10:26,800 --> 00:10:28,600
So he arranged this?

181
00:10:30,050 --> 00:10:31,950
Okay, let's say it's like what you said.

182
00:10:32,740 --> 00:10:34,370
The Cause and Effect Correction Bureau

183
00:10:34,540 --> 00:10:36,570
is a body responsible
for correcting the cause and effect.

184
00:10:36,740 --> 00:10:37,930
Then they should be correcting matters

185
00:10:38,370 --> 00:10:40,170
after something has happened

186
00:10:40,310 --> 00:10:41,490
to patch things up.

187
00:10:42,370 --> 00:10:44,050
But from these notes,

188
00:10:44,570 --> 00:10:45,100
it clearly shows

189
00:10:45,190 --> 00:10:47,260
that they preplanned
a lot of things that happened.

190
00:10:50,210 --> 00:10:51,790
Don't you think it's strange?

191
00:10:55,790 --> 00:10:56,760
I'll get some tissues.

192
00:11:01,380 --> 00:11:01,870
Are you okay?

193
00:11:04,370 --> 00:11:06,570
Grandma, you should lie down

194
00:11:06,660 --> 00:11:08,200
after finishing the fruit.

195
00:11:08,290 --> 00:11:09,300
It's better to lie down.

196
00:11:10,270 --> 00:11:11,410
I don't want to lie down.

197
00:11:12,650 --> 00:11:14,760
I'll feel worse
if I lie down for too long.

198
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:18,630
The doctor reminded me.

199
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:20,480
You were unconscious for many days.

200
00:11:20,610 --> 00:11:21,440
So you should try to lie down...

201
00:11:21,580 --> 00:11:22,590
What do they know?

202
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:26,330
They weren't the ones
who cured my illness.

203
00:11:32,490 --> 00:11:34,950
I've been a Sikawasay for years.

204
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:38,430
How could I not know

205
00:11:38,960 --> 00:11:40,360
why I got sick?

206
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:43,620
How could I not know

207
00:11:44,280 --> 00:11:46,080
who healed me?

208
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:57,220
I saw you before I woke up.

209
00:12:02,280 --> 00:12:04,520
I saw you holding my hand.

210
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:09,100
Then shiny little lights

211
00:12:09,230 --> 00:12:11,690
were floating all over the place.

212
00:12:19,440 --> 00:12:20,930
Grandma.

213
00:12:23,220 --> 00:12:25,510
There were so many of them.

214
00:12:26,560 --> 00:12:27,840
It was just like when I taught you

215
00:12:27,930 --> 00:12:30,210
the Ceremony of Connection.

216
00:12:30,430 --> 00:12:31,490
It was the same.

217
00:12:31,890 --> 00:12:33,820
The same shiny lights.

218
00:12:42,090 --> 00:12:44,820
What matters is that you're awake now.

219
00:12:47,550 --> 00:12:48,390
Grandma.

220
00:12:48,520 --> 00:12:50,500
I don't know when you'll be discharged,

221
00:12:50,590 --> 00:12:52,170
but I've been thinking.

222
00:12:52,300 --> 00:12:53,970
When you've gotten enough rest,

223
00:12:54,110 --> 00:12:55,780
I'll schedule something.

224
00:12:56,090 --> 00:12:58,330
Let's go somewhere together. Okay?

225
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:02,820
Where do you want to take me?

226
00:13:04,670 --> 00:13:05,680
It's up to you.

227
00:13:06,070 --> 00:13:09,590
You can decide
if you want to go sightseeing,

228
00:13:09,730 --> 00:13:10,610
eat delicious food,

229
00:13:10,740 --> 00:13:12,280
or visit any place you want.

230
00:13:13,380 --> 00:13:15,230
I want to go home.

231
00:13:16,330 --> 00:13:17,650
You want to go home?

232
00:13:18,530 --> 00:13:20,860
Okay, I'll go home with you.

233
00:13:22,220 --> 00:13:24,420
Then we can go to the beach.

234
00:13:24,640 --> 00:13:26,140
We will go see the dolphins.

235
00:13:26,970 --> 00:13:27,850
Will that be okay?

236
00:13:28,340 --> 00:13:29,000
Dolphins?

237
00:13:29,130 --> 00:13:29,610
Yes.

238
00:13:29,740 --> 00:13:30,980
We'll have to use a boat.

239
00:13:31,900 --> 00:13:34,230
I'll arrange something
that's not too tiring.

240
00:13:34,850 --> 00:13:35,510
All right?

241
00:13:41,490 --> 00:13:43,250
The quarantined patient in room 701

242
00:13:43,380 --> 00:13:44,700
is having complications!

243
00:13:44,790 --> 00:13:46,160
Backup required!

244
00:13:47,560 --> 00:13:48,660
Call the doctor.

245
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:50,600
The patient is in critical condition.

246
00:13:50,910 --> 00:13:52,400
Have you informed the family?

247
00:14:05,030 --> 00:14:07,190
[Timeline number 05331.]

248
00:14:07,360 --> 00:14:08,990
[Send a modification agent]

249
00:14:09,080 --> 00:14:10,880
[to Hsieh Tien-ti's new school]

250
00:14:11,150 --> 00:14:13,350
[to find out
what the students think of her.]

251
00:14:13,440 --> 00:14:14,710
[I'll teach them a lesson.]

252
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:18,060
No, it's okay. They're right.

253
00:14:18,230 --> 00:14:20,120
I don't have a mom or a dad.

254
00:14:20,480 --> 00:14:22,280
Grandma doesn't want me either.

255
00:14:26,190 --> 00:14:28,260
But I know

256
00:14:28,390 --> 00:14:30,770
that I'm not a loser or a jinx.

257
00:14:32,050 --> 00:14:33,100
Because compared to them,

258
00:14:33,230 --> 00:14:35,480
I'm much luckier.

259
00:14:38,290 --> 00:14:39,040
[In conclusion,]

260
00:14:39,130 --> 00:14:41,420
[the messenger, 'Orad,
is becoming closer to Hsieh Tien-ti.]

261
00:14:41,510 --> 00:14:43,180
[Everything is going as planned.]

262
00:14:45,820 --> 00:14:48,460
[Timeline number 22145.]

263
00:14:48,990 --> 00:14:50,310
[Send a memory modification agent]

264
00:14:50,390 --> 00:14:51,890
[to Hsieh Tien-ti's school.]

265
00:14:52,150 --> 00:14:54,220
[Let the teacher tell the story
of a rainy doll,]

266
00:14:54,400 --> 00:14:56,770
[leading her
to give the messenger a present.]

267
00:14:57,130 --> 00:14:59,150
[Who wants it to rain every day?]

268
00:15:00,780 --> 00:15:01,350
There is someone.

269
00:15:02,760 --> 00:15:03,590
Me.

270
00:15:04,300 --> 00:15:06,060
Why do you want it to rain every day?

271
00:15:09,530 --> 00:15:13,010
If it rains every day,

272
00:15:13,100 --> 00:15:16,880
then I'll be able

273
00:15:17,810 --> 00:15:20,620
to see you all the time.

274
